{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MCPMPdC8gdm4w7efiTu9L9","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"96a7237f4ef0dea296a9e6b3a8c67b3837a8ad82\",\"date\":\"2026-10-15T16:32:00-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2828)\",\"refs\":\"HEAD\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"ee87f30cbee9346257c3479aa57a4e1a15d21e1a\",\"date\":\"2026-10-15T11:43:55Z\",\"message\":\"(chore) Release v12.1.1\",\"refs\":\"tag: v12.1.1\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"3a2dcee575c8cbeba7096aeb0ee37c8c514705bd\",\"date\":\"2026-10-15T10:44:08Z\",\"message\":\"(chore) Release v12.1.0\",\"refs\":\"tag: v12.1.0\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"ba4b122d13859015fe9dca89b5b343baf363590b\",\"date\":\"2026-10-14T16:34:40-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2826)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"a7bd67168e3db4b095f8a1c06451549d3ec77b79\",\"date\":\"2026-10-14T19:25:14+05:30\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-6098: Show today's appointments and visit attribute tags in the current visit summary (#2824)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"6bb8b739e7d8e0b529399fca9f19d7a08cee3509\",\"date\":\"2026-10-10T10:29:23-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Switch to using NPM trusted-publication\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6d5cdfcb9a18050ba06f5d84cd3d4dd8bbb2338f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-08T09:05:04Z\",\"message\":\"(chore) Release v12.0.0\",\"refs\":\"tag: v12.0.0\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"f33b707088c8177357e39b08fc6fcc34b8d3d040\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T16:36:52-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2812)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"fce33d7cfabd0d71ec93dafba9bc501b5973f79f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T19:11:46+05:30\",\"message\":\"(chore) Bump esm-framework peerDependency to 11.x (#2815)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"d3e81d99a314ba62c08851cd5df1e44dfcfe4506\",\"date\":\"2026-10-06T16:21:45+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Add a page header to the service queues admin page (#2806)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"ff624012f906133cc0594d87e89063b9cf85463f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T13:48:19+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5666: Handle Call action failures in the queue table (#2789)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-5666: Handle Call action failures in the queue table\\n\\nThe Call row action and the Serve button in the call modal both post to\\nqueueutil/assignticket without handling a rejection, so a failed request\\nbecame an unhandled promise rejection: a full-screen error overlay in\\ndevelopment builds and a click that did nothing in production.\\n\\nCatch the Call request's failure and show an error snackbar with the\\nserver's message, falling back to a generic one. Give the Serve modal's\\nticket display request its own rejection handler. By then the queue\\nentry has already been transitioned, so say that, close the modal and\\nrefresh the queue.\\n\\n* Show the server's message in the Serve modal's other error handlers\\n\\nThe Serve and Requeue failure handlers passed error.message to the\\nsnackbar, which is the fetch wrapper's \\\"Server responded with 500 ...\\\"\\nrather than the message the server sent. Use getErrorMessage with the\\ngeneric fallback, matching the ticket display handler in the same modal\\nand the other queue entry modals.\\n\\n* Assert the queue refresh in the call modal's ticket display failure test\\n\\nShare the mutateQueueEntries mock in the call modal tests so the ticket\\ndisplay failure test can assert that the queue entries are refreshed after\\nthe modal closes.\\n\\nAlso drop the toBeEnabled assertion from the Call action failure test.\\nNothing disables the Call button, so the assertion could never fail.\\n\\n* Navigate to the patient chart when the ticket display update fails\\n\\nWhen serving a patient, the queue entry is transitioned before the ticket\\ndisplay is updated. If the ticket display request fails, the patient has\\nstill moved on in the queue, so take the user to the patient chart the\\nsame way the success path does instead of leaving them on the queue\\nscreen. The error snackbar is rendered by the app shell, so it stays\\nvisible after navigating.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"ee5de808d2e20e1d15e79b4e90c8e0b6ed19746c\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T22:03:17+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5666: Show plain-text server errors in queue snackbars (#2800)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-5666: Show plain-text server errors in queue snackbars\\n\\ngetErrorMessage now returns the response body when the server sends a\\nplain-text error, instead of falling through to err.message.\\n\\nWhen a response isn't JSON, openmrsFetch sets responseBody to the raw\\ntext. Some queue module endpoints send plain-text 400s, such as\\nPOST /queueutil/assignticket returning \\\"One of the required fields is\\nempty\\\". Snackbars were showing the generic OpenmrsFetchError message\\n(\\\"Server responded with 400 (Bad Request) for url ...\\\") instead.\\n\\nProxy error pages (like an nginx 502/504) also arrive as a string\\nresponseBody, so the body is only used when it's non-empty, 500\\ncharacters or fewer, and contains no markup. Otherwise we fall back to\\nerr.message as before. Structured JSON error fields still take priority.\\n\\n* Add a test for the plain-text error length cap\\n\\nCovers the case where a plain-text responseBody is longer than the\\n500-character cap, which should fall back to err.message instead of\\nshowing the body in a snackbar.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4e54575a12fcdac16931f001de5ab8e5804b624a\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T20:57:41+05:30\",\"message\":\"Merge branch 'main' into visit-notes-form-type\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"610a1d7a6a0732137f289840acb800e25ed6fa8c\",\"date\":\"2026-09-30T16:36:26-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2797)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"6f362b0a9082262455d6739ca57ed1fe618cc414\",\"date\":\"2026-09-30T15:00:46-04:00\",\"message\":\"Update packages/esm-service-queues-app/src/current-visit/current-visit-summary.test.tsx\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"chibongho\",\"authorEmail\":\"cbho@pih.org\"},{\"hash\":\"38a12398be5b1e9b89b40521db3353e17df68c79\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T17:44:14-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-6020: Change visit summary in queues app to pass in correct encounter object\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Chi Bong Ho\",\"authorEmail\":\"cbho@pih.org\"},{\"hash\":\"8eff6bab5486b7773d3cb7aa17e4cc310fa7715d\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T01:58:55+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Declare react-dom as a peer dependency (#2784)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Add react-dom 18.x to peerDependencies in the bed management, patient list management, patient registration, patient search, service queues, and ward apps.\\n\\nThe app shell provides react-dom through module federation, but the\\nOpenMRS rspack config only shares the dependencies an app lists in\\npeerDependencies. Without react-dom listed there, the app loads the\\ncopy of react-dom bundled into its own build instead of the shell's.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"02b9b6ca64a4188e81eea405b88a62ea4208fc2a\",\"date\":\"2026-09-27T00:48:19+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) O3-5859: Add @carbon/react to peerDependencies (#2779)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Declare @carbon/react as a 1.x peer in eight patient-management apps so the build tooling shares it with the app shell instead of bundling a separate copy.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2a738e85b62f1a6d31412b92c9e654d5e089702b\",\"date\":\"2026-09-23T16:33:44-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2771)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"aeefd9d539435790431fc346de5ad6439d9fd7f4\",\"date\":\"2026-09-22T16:31:35-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2768)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"c2d4b9fc2937b12a5dcf09d55d509c3a4abfac77\",\"date\":\"2026-09-22T23:35:08+08:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5997: Make service queues metric values less shouty (#2766)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-5997: Make service queues metric values less shouty\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5997: Unbold the metric tile header labels\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5997: Match the header label style used in the other metrics strip\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"7dc40adfde68677979aa9422d5d00858a8213121\",\"date\":\"2026-09-22T20:54:37+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5983: Add the actions menu back to in-service patient cards (#2752)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-5983: Add the actions menu back to in-service patient cards\\n\\nThe in-service cards on the queue page replaced the table rows that carried\\nthe Move, Edit, Remove patient and Undo transition actions, so those actions\\nwere lost.\\n\\nEach card now has an overflow menu in its top-right corner with those four\\nactions, reusing the queue table's action menu items so the handlers, labels\\nand visibility rules stay in one place. The menu sits outside the patient\\nchart link so opening it does not navigate away.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5983: Render queue actions as direct menu items and move the card menu beside the link\\n\\nCarbon's OverflowMenu clones each direct child with the ref and focus handlers its keyboard navigation relies on. The shared wrapper component dropped them, so arrow keys did not move between items in the card menu or the queue table. Replace the wrapper with a hook that returns the visible OverflowMenuItems directly.\\n\\nMark the shared remove action as a delete action to match its danger confirmation button.\\n\\nPlace the card's actions menu beside the patient chart link instead of over it, so the two hit areas do not overlap. The service row extends under the menu column so its divider still reaches the card edge.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5983: Move the card actions menu into the queue status bar, outside the patient chart link\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"71b3d3f10534189eafd4786628aeceecdb4a84c2\",\"date\":\"2026-09-21T22:24:56+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) O3-5924: Use React-scoped JSX types (#2763)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Replace global JSX.Element references with React.JSX.Element in registration, service queues and the admission workspace.\\n\\nPrepare for React 19 types without changing the React 18 runtime or JSX build configuration.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d6ca1f1c04e431bcaa7c79d46fd9027639db49eb\",\"date\":\"2026-09-21T18:04:19+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Adopt the shared Prettier configuration (#2764)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* chore: Adopt the shared Prettier configuration\\n\\nUse @openmrs/prettier-config in the existing config wrapper and pin Prettier to 3.9.8. Keep our bracketSameLine override.\\n\\n* Apply Prettier 3.9.8 formatting\\n\\nApply the measured indentation change in the service queues config schema. Leave existing formatting issues elsewhere untouched.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c741c18000e41edbaefa3266b184c26507835735\",\"date\":\"2026-09-18T16:31:14-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2760)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"}],\"totalCount\":94}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e63859dc-c8bb-4788-b23c-85c165ed2c8c","uuid":"2d451af7-78b2-47db-ba42-19a4382e7f32","timestamp":"2026-10-23T15:13:52.530Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"96a7237f4ef0dea296a9e6b3a8c67b3837a8ad82\",\"date\":\"2026-10-15T16:32:00-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2828)\",\"refs\":\"HEAD\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"ee87f30cbee9346257c3479aa57a4e1a15d21e1a\",\"date\":\"2026-10-15T11:43:55Z\",\"message\":\"(chore) Release v12.1.1\",\"refs\":\"tag: v12.1.1\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"3a2dcee575c8cbeba7096aeb0ee37c8c514705bd\",\"date\":\"2026-10-15T10:44:08Z\",\"message\":\"(chore) Release v12.1.0\",\"refs\":\"tag: v12.1.0\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"ba4b122d13859015fe9dca89b5b343baf363590b\",\"date\":\"2026-10-14T16:34:40-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2826)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"a7bd67168e3db4b095f8a1c06451549d3ec77b79\",\"date\":\"2026-10-14T19:25:14+05:30\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-6098: Show today's appointments and visit attribute tags in the current visit summary (#2824)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"6bb8b739e7d8e0b529399fca9f19d7a08cee3509\",\"date\":\"2026-10-10T10:29:23-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Switch to using NPM trusted-publication\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6d5cdfcb9a18050ba06f5d84cd3d4dd8bbb2338f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-08T09:05:04Z\",\"message\":\"(chore) Release v12.0.0\",\"refs\":\"tag: v12.0.0\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"f33b707088c8177357e39b08fc6fcc34b8d3d040\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T16:36:52-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2812)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"fce33d7cfabd0d71ec93dafba9bc501b5973f79f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T19:11:46+05:30\",\"message\":\"(chore) Bump esm-framework peerDependency to 11.x (#2815)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"d3e81d99a314ba62c08851cd5df1e44dfcfe4506\",\"date\":\"2026-10-06T16:21:45+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Add a page header to the service queues admin page (#2806)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"ff624012f906133cc0594d87e89063b9cf85463f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T13:48:19+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5666: Handle Call action failures in the queue table (#2789)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-5666: Handle Call action failures in the queue table\\n\\nThe Call row action and the Serve button in the call modal both post to\\nqueueutil/assignticket without handling a rejection, so a failed request\\nbecame an unhandled promise rejection: a full-screen error overlay in\\ndevelopment builds and a click that did nothing in production.\\n\\nCatch the Call request's failure and show an error snackbar with the\\nserver's message, falling back to a generic one. Give the Serve modal's\\nticket display request its own rejection handler. By then the queue\\nentry has already been transitioned, so say that, close the modal and\\nrefresh the queue.\\n\\n* Show the server's message in the Serve modal's other error handlers\\n\\nThe Serve and Requeue failure handlers passed error.message to the\\nsnackbar, which is the fetch wrapper's \\\"Server responded with 500 ...\\\"\\nrather than the message the server sent. Use getErrorMessage with the\\ngeneric fallback, matching the ticket display handler in the same modal\\nand the other queue entry modals.\\n\\n* Assert the queue refresh in the call modal's ticket display failure test\\n\\nShare the mutateQueueEntries mock in the call modal tests so the ticket\\ndisplay failure test can assert that the queue entries are refreshed after\\nthe modal closes.\\n\\nAlso drop the toBeEnabled assertion from the Call action failure test.\\nNothing disables the Call button, so the assertion could never fail.\\n\\n* Navigate to the patient chart when the ticket display update fails\\n\\nWhen serving a patient, the queue entry is transitioned before the ticket\\ndisplay is updated. If the ticket display request fails, the patient has\\nstill moved on in the queue, so take the user to the patient chart the\\nsame way the success path does instead of leaving them on the queue\\nscreen. The error snackbar is rendered by the app shell, so it stays\\nvisible after navigating.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"ee5de808d2e20e1d15e79b4e90c8e0b6ed19746c\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T22:03:17+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5666: Show plain-text server errors in queue snackbars (#2800)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-5666: Show plain-text server errors in queue snackbars\\n\\ngetErrorMessage now returns the response body when the server sends a\\nplain-text error, instead of falling through to err.message.\\n\\nWhen a response isn't JSON, openmrsFetch sets responseBody to the raw\\ntext. Some queue module endpoints send plain-text 400s, such as\\nPOST /queueutil/assignticket returning \\\"One of the required fields is\\nempty\\\". Snackbars were showing the generic OpenmrsFetchError message\\n(\\\"Server responded with 400 (Bad Request) for url ...\\\") instead.\\n\\nProxy error pages (like an nginx 502/504) also arrive as a string\\nresponseBody, so the body is only used when it's non-empty, 500\\ncharacters or fewer, and contains no markup. Otherwise we fall back to\\nerr.message as before. Structured JSON error fields still take priority.\\n\\n* Add a test for the plain-text error length cap\\n\\nCovers the case where a plain-text responseBody is longer than the\\n500-character cap, which should fall back to err.message instead of\\nshowing the body in a snackbar.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4e54575a12fcdac16931f001de5ab8e5804b624a\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T20:57:41+05:30\",\"message\":\"Merge branch 'main' into visit-notes-form-type\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"610a1d7a6a0732137f289840acb800e25ed6fa8c\",\"date\":\"2026-09-30T16:36:26-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2797)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"6f362b0a9082262455d6739ca57ed1fe618cc414\",\"date\":\"2026-09-30T15:00:46-04:00\",\"message\":\"Update packages/esm-service-queues-app/src/current-visit/current-visit-summary.test.tsx\",\"r